<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
    <title><%= content_for(:subject) || "Tastatur" %></title>
  </head>

  <%#
    Email is not the web. Everything here is deliberate and none of it should be
    "modernised":

    - Inline styles on every element. Gmail strips <style> blocks and Outlook
      ignores most of what survives.
    - Table layout, not flexbox or grid. Outlook renders through Word's engine,
      which supports neither.
    - No web font. Archivo cannot be loaded in most clients, so the stack falls
      back to the Helvetica/Arial lineage the brand descends from, which is a far
      closer match than a serif default.
    - No background images, no rounded corners, no shadows. The paper-and-
      hairline aesthetic happens to be exactly what email renders reliably.
    - Light only. Dark-mode email means fighting each client's own inversion
      heuristics, which is not a fight worth having.
  %>
  <body style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#f2f1ec;">
    <!-- Preheader: the grey text a client shows beside the subject line. -->
    <div style="display:none; font-size:1px; color:#f2f1ec; line-height:1px; max-height:0; max-width:0; opacity:0; overflow:hidden;">
      <%= yield :preheader %>
    </div>

    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
           style="background-color:#f2f1ec;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding:32px 16px;">

          <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                 style="max-width:520px; width:100%;">

            <!-- Wordmark, with the accent square from the app header. -->
            <tr>
              <td style="padding-bottom:20px;">
                <span style="font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px;
                             font-weight:700; letter-spacing:3.5px; text-transform:uppercase;
                             color:#16150f;">Tastatur</span>
                <span style="display:inline-block; width:7px; height:7px; background-color:#c1440e;
                             margin-left:6px; line-height:7px;">&nbsp;</span>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!-- The card: 1px hairline on paper, no radius, no shadow. -->
            <tr>
              <td style="background-color:#fcfcfa; border:1px solid #e3e1d8; padding:32px;
                         font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
                         font-size:15px; line-height:1.55; color:#16150f;">
                <%= yield %>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td style="padding-top:20px; font-family:'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
                         font-size:12px; line-height:1.6; color:#8c8a80;">
                Cookieless web analytics.
                <a href="<%= Tastatur.base_url %>/privacy"
                   style="color:#8c8a80; text-decoration:underline;">What we collect</a>
                &middot;
                <a href="<%= Tastatur.base_url %>/docs"
                   style="color:#8c8a80; text-decoration:underline;">Documentation</a>
                <br>
                You are receiving this because someone used this address on
                <%= ENV.fetch("APP_HOST", "localhost:3000") %>. If that was not
                you, ignore this message and nothing will happen.
              </td>
            </tr>

          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
